Vega-Lite allows you to set a font family globally using the `config` property. You can specify the font family for all text elements, including titles, labels, and captions, by setting the `font` property within the `config.view` or `config.axis`, `config.title`, `config.legend` objects, or more generally with `config.text`. However, for a more comprehensive change, you can use `config.view.labelFont` and other similar properties or set `config.text.font` to apply it to most text elements. 

For example, you can add the following configuration to your Vega-Lite specification to set the font family globally:
```json
"config": {
  "text": {"font": "Source Sans Pro"},
  "title": {"font": "Source Sans Pro"},
  "axis": {"labelFont": "Source Sans Pro", "titleFont": "Source Sans Pro"},
  "legend": {"labelFont": "Source Sans Pro", "titleFont": "Source Sans Pro"}
}
```
However, a simpler way is to directly set the font size and family for specific elements like title and axis labels as needed. For a uniform look, you might want to explore setting it at the view or text config level.

To set the font size to 11pt, you can similarly adjust the `config` or specific elements like `title.fontSize`. For instance:
```json
"config": {
  "text": {"fontSize": 11, "font": "Source Sans Pro"}
}
```

